    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter tonight\u2019s slate with a lineup anchored by two high-efficiency leadoff hitters: **Christian Yelich** (74.33) and **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (72.03). **Christian Yelich** benefits from an excellent matchup against the 4.54 xERA of McGreevy, where his dynamic platoon advantage and high spot in the order provide the day's highest ceiling. Meanwhile, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** leverages a massive 16% park boost against Kremer; while the SP skill adjustment is negative, his ability to capitalize on speed in a favorable hitting environment makes him an elite play. We are also looking for significant production from **Josh Smith** (64.66) and **Dillon Dingler** (63.75), both of whom benefit from favorable SP xERAs and prime spots in the #2 hole, maximizing their opportunities to drive runs in the early innings.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision involved **Carson Benge** (43.82) and **Nelson Velazquez** (41.88), both of whom hovered near the marginal threshold but ultimately fell short of the starting cut. **Carson Benge** was the closest to inclusion, but his overall efficiency score failed to clear the bar set by **Luke Raley** (59.62), whose matchup against Phillips offers a superior blend of SP xERA favorability and platoon positioning. **Nelson Velazquez** was handicapped by a tough matchup against Harrison and a lack of the high-leverage context that elevated the rest of the outfield. We have opted to bench both to preserve our seasonal game caps, as their raw scores simply didn't provide enough separation from our primary starters to justify the usage.\n\nRisk management remains a priority given the caliber of arms on the mound tonight. **Casey Schmitt** (45.19) and **Kyle Schwarber** (52.05) face significant hurdles, with the former battling the elite stuff of Cease and the latter facing a difficult strikeout threat in Burns. While we expect **Yordan Alvarez** (60.44) to provide stable production, his platoon disadvantage against Griffin slightly lowers his floor compared to his usual elite status. Keep a close eye on **Kazuma Okamoto** (49.64) and **Chase Meidroth** (50.55); while they are starting, their low-50s scores indicate limited upside against Webb and Bennett. We are holding **Trea Turner**, **Hyeseong Kim**, **Colt Keith**, **Lars Nootbaar**, **Gary Sanchez**, **Pedro Ramirez**, **Luis Pena**, and **Jacob Gonzalez** in reserve today, prioritizing lineup depth and efficiency over raw volume.",
